fragment:
- The parameters should be generated by LLM according to the context. - The explanation for each action should be generated by LLM according to the context in which that action was chosen (reason, sequence, etc.). - "action_id" is not seuential identifier, it must match the number in parentheses of the chosen action. Exemples: SET_TEXT (3) == "action_id": "3" CLICK (4) == "action_id": "4" LONG_CLICK (2) == "action_id": "2" BACK (5) == "action_id": "5"
Your response MUST follow this schema - a JSON object with the following structure: { "actions": [ { "action_id": "5", "action_text": "CLICK (5)", "params": {}, "explanation": "Why this action is included in the batch" }, { "action_id": "2", "action_text": "SET_TEXT (2)", "params": {"text": "test@example.com"}, "explanation": "Why this action logically follows the previous one" } // Additional related actions... ], "batch_explanation": "Overall explanation of why these actions form a logical batch" }
DO NOT include any additional text outside of the JSON object. Your response must be valid JSON that can be parsed directly.
